      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 19th‑century coal seam powered Inverness; a railway and pier built by William Penn Hussey shipped coal to Europe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverness%2C_Nova_Scotia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After Hussey, William Mackenzie and Donald Mann expanded mining, opening shafts that later became the site of Cabot Links golf course.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverness%2C_Nova_Scotia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Inverness Raceway, founded in 1926, still hosts harness races twice weekly during the summer months.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverness%2C_Nova_Scotia",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Cabot Links, opened in 2011 on former mine shafts, earned a Golf Digest world ranking of 43rd in 2018.",
